comments.body:
fix up in #48901.

Root cause turned out to be a bit different from the async-copy theory: it's an interaction between `torch.compile` and **chunked prefill** specifically — the pooled last-token hidden state reads a reused/aliased buffer whose producing kernel hasn't completed for the partial-prefill shape. It reproduces only when both are on (`--enforce-eager` is always correct; a single-chunk prompt is always correct), which matches why offline `LLM.score()` looked fine.

@ravenZ3 thanks for offering to help. if you're able to try #48901 against your original case (long query+doc, chunked prefill, compile on) and confirm it resolves the issue you saw, that'd be a useful second data point.
